    // 'this.#x': a private name. It is stored under the MANGLED key '__#<body>#x',
    // exactly as both compiler halves store it (privKey in js-to-llvm-ir.abnf), and for
    // the same three reasons: the '__' prefix is this engine's marker for a slot that no
    // enumeration reports, so a private field stays out of for-in, Object.keys and
    // object spread the way a real private name does; it keeps `o["#x"] = 1` and a
    // private `#x` in DIFFERENT slots; and the '<body>' component is the CLASS BODY the
    // name is declared in, because a private name is scoped to its class body and not
    // to its spelling - `class A { #v }` and `class B extends A { #v }` declare TWO
    // names in node. isPrivateKey is what lets the class-side lookups still see it,
    // since it is a '__' name they otherwise skip.
    //
